  "manufactures_distress": false,
  "at_matched_length": "the tape's -0.0158 sits at the 38th percentile of block-50 paths; median simulated -0.0144. The simulator draws slightly MILDER troughs than the one path that happened, not deeper ones.",
  "but_the_block_length_is_doing_the_work": "iid resampling gives a median drawdown of -0.0035 and a 0.5% completion rate at the tape's length; block 50 gives -0.0144 and 20%. The drawdown the report quotes is a property of the 50-block splice, and 50 is the value that matches the tape, which is evidence for it rather than against.",
  "power": "one path, one draw. It sits mid-distribution, so it neither rejects the model nor confirms it: a single observation cannot estimate the simulator's error, and the 0.1% death tail rests on 0-1 events out of 900 paths, which the tape can never check because the tape never died.",
